---
title: Configuration
description: Every option in the nimbus.yaml configuration file.
---

# Configuration

{% $product %} reads its settings from `nimbus.yaml`. On Windows, the file is located in `%APPDATA%\Nimbus`; on macOS and Linux, in `~/.config/nimbus`.

## Example configuration

```yaml {% title="nimbus.yaml" lines=true %}
server: https://sync.example.com
account: jane.doe@example.com

folders:
  - path: ~/Projects
    exclude: ["node_modules", "*.tmp"]
  - path: ~/Documents/Contracts
    versions: 50

bandwidth:
  upload: 20mbit
  download: unlimited

updates:
  channel: stable
```

## General options

| Option | Type | Default | Description |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| `server` | URL | – | Address of the Nimbus server |
| `account` | String | – | Account used to sign in |
| `folders` | List | `[]` | Folders to keep in sync |
| `bandwidth.upload` | Rate | `unlimited` | Upload limit |
| `updates.channel` | `stable` / `beta` | `stable` | Update channel |

{% details title="Advanced options" %}
| Option | Default | Description |
|:---|:---|:---|
| `scan.interval` | `300` | Seconds between full scans |
| `log.level` | `info` | `error`, `warn`, `info` or `debug` |
| `proxy` | System | Proxy server, e.g. `http://proxy:3128` |
{% /details %}

## Encryption {% #encryption %}

On first launch, the client generates a key pair. The private key is protected by your password and stored in the operating system's keychain.{% footnote %}On Linux, the Secret Service API is used – for example GNOME Keyring or KWallet.{% /footnote %}

{% callout type="danger" title="Keep your recovery key safe" %}
If the private key is lost and there is no recovery key, the encrypted data cannot be recovered. Print the recovery key and store it in a secure place.
{% /callout %}

## Limiting bandwidth

{% $product %} shares the available bandwidth evenly among all active transfers. With a limit of 20 Mbit/s, uploading 1 GB takes about seven minutes. Keep this in mind when [setting up your first folder](installation.mdoc#first-folder): large folders are best added outside working hours.
